<!--
	Neutralizes the automatic merge target that ILRepack.Lib.MSBuild.Task injects
	into every Release build of a project referencing it.

	The package's build/ILRepack.Lib.MSBuild.Task.targets defines
	<Target Name="ILRepack" AfterTargets="Build"> guarded by
	`!Exists('$(ILRepackTargetsFile)')`. When no such file exists, that target
	merges the primary output with EVERY DLL in the output directory
	(TargetKind="SameAsPrimaryAssembly") and then deletes the copy-local files.

	For Selva.gha that meant System.Drawing.Common and the bodiless
	System.Windows.Forms reference assembly were merged into the plugin, so
	ILRepack rewrote Grasshopper member references like
	AddCategoryIcon(String, System.Drawing.Bitmap) to point at the internalized
	Bitmap copy — a different type identity than the one Grasshopper.dll
	declares. Result: MissingMethodException the moment the plugin loads
	(shipped in 0.17.1). Debug builds were unaffected because the auto-target is
	Release-only, which is exactly why it went unnoticed.

	Directory.Build.props points ILRepackTargetsFile here, so the Exists() check
	succeeds, the auto-target's condition is false, and this (empty) project is
	imported instead. The intended merges live in explicit targets in
	Selva.GH.csproj and Selva.Drawing.csproj, with hand-picked inputs.
-->
<Project>
</Project>
